#
# Release-signing public keys every TT Station agent trusts, compiled in
# (crates/tt-station-agentd/src/release_keys.rs). An update is installed only
# if its package carries a valid signature from one of these, or from a key
# in the box's own update channel file (docs/reference/releases.md).
#
# One key per line: `<name> <base64 of the 32-byte Ed25519 public key>`.
# Names are what logs and refusals show; use `tt-station-<year><letter>`.
# Rotating: add the new key here, ship a release signed with the OLD key that
# carries both, then switch the release secret; remove the old key a release
# or two later (docs/reference/releases.md, "Rotating a key").
#
# Empty until the release key holder is decided: with no keys here, a box
# installs only releases signed by keys its owner has added to the channel
# file. The release workflow refuses to publish packages whose signature
# doesn't check out against this file.
